#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198077 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37b088db-dca6-50cd-8af9-b057545eb87b" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Linear Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "33efc452-774d-50e9-94b5-215c9c117fec" :question/math-academy-id "e-13143" :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A = \\{n \\in \\mathbb{N}: 5n - 2 \\leq 21 \\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $5n - 2 \\leq 21.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5n-2 & \\le 21 \\\\ 5n & \\le 23 \\\\ n & \\le \\frac{23}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe positive integer solutions of the inequality above are $1,2,3,4.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA = \\{1,2,3,4\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198087 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739c04ac-6d0c-5173-aa91-b5cc4dec8128" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Quadratic Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "88362b76-a41c-590b-9252-264c2bd4fcfe" :question/math-academy-id "e-13176" :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{Z}: x^2 - 9 \\lt 0\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $x^2 - 9 < 0.$\n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-9 & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & <9 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{9} \\\\ |x| & <3 \\\\ -3<x & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the inequality above are $0,\\pm1,\\pm2.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA = \\{ 0, \\pm 1, \\pm 2\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198088 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2ae57a-fde8-5d07-bbff-e66fbd4428b0" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Absolute Value Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "9518a07d-cf1c-51f1-9bac-7634caabc19a" :question/math-academy-id "e-13178" :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A=\\{k \\in \\mathbb{Z}: |k-1| \\leq 4 \\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $|k-1| \\leq 4.$ So, we first need to solve for $k{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|k-1|\\le 4 \\\\ -4\\le k-1\\le 4 \\\\ -3\\le k\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the above inequality are $-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5.$ \n\nTherefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA = \\{0,\\pm1,\\pm2,\\pm3,4,5 \\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198089 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74611c25-8501-52a7-a705-b7e9f8f6b8ee" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Trigonometric Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "21d6faa8-9340-5fad-8bf3-07ce92c449d6" :question/math-academy-id "e-13179" :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A = \\left\\{ x\\in \\mathbb R \\: :\\:  \\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0  \\right\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi x}{2} & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in\\mathbb Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx = 0,\\, \\pm 2 ,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA= \\{0,\\, \\pm 2 ,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37b088db-dca6-50cd-8af9-b057545eb87b" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Linear Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0190de29-8f4e-5a74-93f7-33cbf33aae38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-5,2,10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299343} {:answer/id #uuid "6913999c-d52c-537c-aade-879e8c34d964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 3,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299344} {:answer/id #uuid "b26c40fb-b533-5c8f-b9e6-550fa95f0904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299345} {:answer/id #uuid "3208b920-d9c8-5e85-bcd8-6b65fe0f891f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,\\pm 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299346} {:answer/id #uuid "b404e695-bd64-52bb-b32d-0169d0b3f6fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b404e695-bd64-52bb-b32d-0169d0b3f6fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299347} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1cc441c-f2b8-5191-aed3-bff2af15254a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "35088702-98d7-583f-be4f-fdccb10ce1cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-180759" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={n\\in Z:5n+25=10}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the equation $5n+25=10.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our equation for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5n+25 & =10 \\\\ 5n & =-15 \\\\ n & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is $n=-3,$ which is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we can write the given set as\n\n$$\nA={-3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37b088db-dca6-50cd-8af9-b057545eb87b" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Linear Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0011048a-901a-5a7a-a6c6-dc8d4f77d216" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{…,-2,-1,0,1,2,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299350} {:answer/id #uuid "140b77d2-e5d7-5757-b3ef-84f734918e5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,1,2,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299351} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd53f81-9372-5a21-9a8d-c2f6bd4a9a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{…,-4,-3,-2,-1,0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299352} {:answer/id #uuid "1da79578-d4eb-5a20-8a63-e77331049297" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-2,-1,0,1,2,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299353} {:answer/id #uuid "fc2b3735-6dcd-5902-bc03-87319757e618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{…,-3,-2,-1,0,1,2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0011048a-901a-5a7a-a6c6-dc8d4f77d216" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{…,-2,-1,0,1,2,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299350} :answer-field/id #uuid "bec99302-e9ee-570d-acda-8837712a02e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d41bd60-ebbc-52b5-b3d5-1bceabcd2855" :question/math-academy-id "q-180766" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $B={n\\in Z:2n-11<-4}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $2n-11<-4.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2n-11 & <-4 \\\\ 2n & <7 \\\\ n & <\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the inequality above are $3,2,1,0,-1,-2,….$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nB={…,-2,-1,0,1,2,3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37b088db-dca6-50cd-8af9-b057545eb87b" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Linear Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "028ccdb0-9792-5cf2-aca4-c2fdbe74073f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4,5,6,7,8,9,10,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299357} {:answer/id #uuid "816be789-7c57-5c48-bee7-f16c86ce7cda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{6,7,8,9,10,11,12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299358} {:answer/id #uuid "9c9a9f0b-f44a-53e4-b4e6-829f8dd508cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{6,7,8,9,10,11,12,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299359} {:answer/id #uuid "c5dd6153-6a6a-588d-924a-ec7764e410b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7,8,9,10,11,12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299360} {:answer/id #uuid "30a82d38-fb60-5b5b-a920-d2a96c1b3343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7,8,9,10,11,12,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30a82d38-fb60-5b5b-a920-d2a96c1b3343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7,8,9,10,11,12,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299361} :answer-field/id #uuid "8815f5f2-a009-553a-9bb2-89180f94e0e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8cc0e13-5537-5035-bfbf-e4d4acd0f118" :question/math-academy-id "q-180769" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $C={n\\in N:24<4n}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $24<4n.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24 & <4n \\\\ 6 & <n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe positive integer solutions of the inequality above are $7,8,9,10,11,12,….$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nC={7,8,9,10,11,12,…}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739c04ac-6d0c-5173-aa91-b5cc4dec8128" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Quadratic Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae8559fb-2d1b-5f54-89f3-3fa2a215f282" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm \\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299364} {:answer/id #uuid "2b5995b1-06ac-510e-86d6-4419d82814d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299365} {:answer/id #uuid "b021be71-e7df-5263-83aa-34c4665210c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm \\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299366} {:answer/id #uuid "d02d277c-3226-553b-94ff-977a662cfd85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299367} {:answer/id #uuid "fda82dc1-4085-5a5e-b54e-20d0a80a5a35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,\\pm \\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae8559fb-2d1b-5f54-89f3-3fa2a215f282" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm \\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299364} :answer-field/id #uuid "6316e1fa-9024-5d6c-bc42-defe888de776" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e7f7a8e-abcf-58c0-b88d-bd9e99c10134" :question/math-academy-id "q-180771" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $B={x\\in R:{x}^{2}-5=0}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are real numbers that satisfy the equation ${x}^{2}-5=0.$\n\nSo, we first need to solve our equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-5 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $x=-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5},$ and both of these solutions are real numbers.\n\nTherefore, we can write the given set as\n\n$$\nB={\\pm \\sqrt{5}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198697 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2ae57a-fde8-5d07-bbff-e66fbd4428b0" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Absolute Value Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff821eae-25ee-5f75-bb04-76c3a7714c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0, ± 1, ± 2, ± 3, ± 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195133} {:answer/id #uuid "13648916-1ee7-54ac-a543-27e31523c835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[- 9, 4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195134} {:answer/id #uuid "21629dfd-ab37-586d-a408-ab31d85b4e33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-9, 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195135} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad194da-c94a-52ce-98ff-94789681618f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{± 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195136} {:answer/id #uuid "745d1120-032e-5146-8bac-3fa81cc16c40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21629dfd-ab37-586d-a408-ab31d85b4e33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-9, 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195135} :answer-field/id #uuid "d664694c-1eac-5607-89ed-808cf7cad072" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b61314af-45e5-5b36-92b8-6af732061931" :question/math-academy-id "q-181117" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:|2x+5|=13}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the real numbers that satisfy the equation $|2x+5|=13.$ So, we first need to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2x+5| & =13 \\\\ 2x+5 & =\\pm 13 \\\\ 2x & =-5\\pm 13 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-5\\pm 13}{2} \\\\ x & =-9,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $x=-9$ and $x=4,$ and both of these solutions are real numbers.\n\nTherefore, we can write the given set as\n\n$$\nA={-9,4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198700 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74611c25-8501-52a7-a705-b7e9f8f6b8ee" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Trigonometric Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da8e8c34-da20-5ec4-bd90-0108be3978f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195172} {:answer/id #uuid "0af72ae5-fec3-5e07-a12f-800f6ad5d00e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0, ± \\frac{1}{2}, ± 1, ± \\frac{3}{2}, …}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195173} {:answer/id #uuid "264eb6a5-0aaa-5ca8-8549-e1c2910b06e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0, ± 1, ± 2, ± 3, …}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195174} {:answer/id #uuid "34c7d578-66a1-5097-b839-6e2515282368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0, \\frac{1}{2}, 1, \\frac{3}{2}, …}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195175} {:answer/id #uuid "78c6d527-dbe7-5bb2-b144-88219a5786f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0af72ae5-fec3-5e07-a12f-800f6ad5d00e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0, ± \\frac{1}{2}, ± 1, ± \\frac{3}{2}, …}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195173} :answer-field/id #uuid "912e2b64-31f9-520b-97fe-a850dcb1399d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ee3e418-5a49-5e58-b433-1b57754ae518" :question/math-academy-id "q-181143" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in Q\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)=0}?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)=0\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi x & =n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =n \\\\ x & =\\frac{n}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={0,\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,…}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74611c25-8501-52a7-a705-b7e9f8f6b8ee" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Trigonometric Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb1d0554-7527-5a3b-9426-c9c6ac152b75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195195} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7a522a-44db-529a-8f8e-38d232329eb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{…,-\\frac{3}{2},-1,-\\frac{1}{2}, 0, \\frac{1}{2}, 1, \\frac{3}{2}, …}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195196} {:answer/id #uuid "106d1858-6afb-5671-9518-50f2c88ef412" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0, \\frac{π}{2}, π, \\frac{3π}{2}, …}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195197} {:answer/id #uuid "2ad2420d-6e86-5fa9-8ee6-a60b42ca9fe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195198} {:answer/id #uuid "71976fc1-fd86-5152-8780-bdb05c00395f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0, ± π, ± 2π, ± 3π, …}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71976fc1-fd86-5152-8780-bdb05c00395f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0, ± π, ± 2π, ± 3π, …}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195199} :answer-field/id #uuid "891ea26c-296f-50f1-af5c-38d8290a913b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8ee30afe-51f8-5f04-a48f-7008842e45fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-181185" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=1\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =n\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,\\pm \\pi ,\\,\\pm 2\\pi ,\\,\\pm 3\\pi ,\\,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,\\pm 3\\pi ,…}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37b088db-dca6-50cd-8af9-b057545eb87b" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Linear Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30d1640e-e30d-5da0-9ef9-6919565d0d88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299371} {:answer/id #uuid "00ae3b0f-f169-5b7c-8236-70541598cecb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299372} {:answer/id #uuid "dba0f78c-9813-5ad5-aa03-8e96a46ee79c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299373} {:answer/id #uuid "aed4b5fc-176a-59c1-9868-f3aa6d575ced" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299374} {:answer/id #uuid "3adf40d8-d046-5e4a-8a42-96f601c628cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dba0f78c-9813-5ad5-aa03-8e96a46ee79c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299373} :answer-field/id #uuid "a11933b5-5ddb-5c5f-b895-796624ffb9b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "54df221d-3d2c-511f-8b47-3eaa34538d89" :question/math-academy-id "q-181755" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={n\\in N:4n+7=-9}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the equation $4n+7=-9.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our equation for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4n+7 & =-9 \\\\ 4n & =-16 \\\\ n & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $-4\\notin N,$ we conclude that the set $A$ contains no elements. Hence, $A=∅.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37b088db-dca6-50cd-8af9-b057545eb87b" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Linear Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b8425b-8958-5775-adb0-81a914e7cdd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299378} {:answer/id #uuid "387ffc18-b928-5848-a38c-89ef181c8fa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299379} {:answer/id #uuid "30027589-1293-5856-8741-909de9198207" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm 1,\\pm 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299380} {:answer/id #uuid "5bf88576-113e-57f1-a55e-b2696a245790" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299381} {:answer/id #uuid "59ec468b-65d1-52d4-87d3-0de21e8dee14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "387ffc18-b928-5848-a38c-89ef181c8fa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299379} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad935293-94f1-5931-9f9a-60b5b51819c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9cfa156b-a24d-57af-8612-d7b64f0445c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-181759" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={n\\in N:3n-5\\le -4}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $3n-5\\le -4.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n-5 & \\le -4 \\\\ 3n & \\le 1 \\\\ n & \\le \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, no natural number satisfies the inequality above. So, we conclude that the set\n$A$ contains no elements. Hence, $A=∅.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299383 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2ae57a-fde8-5d07-bbff-e66fbd4428b0" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Absolute Value Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f0f6559-0a9f-5713-b077-055fc1c69ddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 3,\\pm 4,\\pm 5,\\pm 6,\\pm 7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299385} {:answer/id #uuid "eb1e01ff-006c-5372-a078-7aef7b13990c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299386} {:answer/id #uuid "13b68b68-a8c8-52e8-9c26-352faf059906" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-1,7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299387} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd0ee4a-f91e-5267-9fc5-afd62362af90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299388} {:answer/id #uuid "f419de2e-df7b-51db-8adf-250b2d94c74e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-1,7]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13b68b68-a8c8-52e8-9c26-352faf059906" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-1,7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299387} :answer-field/id #uuid "1186983f-6d44-5880-b421-d4c13441aa4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3e20caf-1664-5be6-9736-621b54e176e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-181761" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:|x-3|=4}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the real numbers that satisfy the equation $|x-3|=4.$ So, we first need to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x-3| & =4 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =3\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =-1,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $x=-1$ and $x=7,$ and both of these solutions are real numbers.\n\nTherefore, we can write the given set as\n\n$$\nA={-1,7}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2ae57a-fde8-5d07-bbff-e66fbd4428b0" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Absolute Value Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97e3cb11-2304-590e-9632-d629c9615eec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299392} {:answer/id #uuid "ab9bc387-d676-5f03-9d1a-f1d8cf22fdae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,1,2,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299393} {:answer/id #uuid "77a00abb-a743-59ac-9667-524a83d77b89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-3,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299394} {:answer/id #uuid "6df691f1-fc80-5e48-94e7-a782a877fc47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299395} {:answer/id #uuid "11832752-77a2-58c6-b665-6a21813b5189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-3,-2,-1,0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77a00abb-a743-59ac-9667-524a83d77b89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-3,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299394} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac962678-b3df-54c8-8888-c71c269041c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34879643-3c0d-5625-9820-47e8669b9a67" :question/math-academy-id "q-181764" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={q\\in Q:|2q|=6}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the rational numbers that satisfy the equation $|2q|=6.$ So, we first need to solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2q| & =6 \\\\ 2q & =\\pm 6 \\\\ q & =\\pm \\frac{6}{2} \\\\ q & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $q=-3$ and $q=3,$ and both of these solutions are rational numbers.\n\nTherefore, we can write the given set as\n\n$$\nA={-3,3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299397 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2ae57a-fde8-5d07-bbff-e66fbd4428b0" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Absolute Value Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3c58495-bd4d-5fac-8931-6288073dcaaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5,6,7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299399} {:answer/id #uuid "0c84f2aa-2f8e-5a59-b160-6da05be9ee04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299400} {:answer/id #uuid "0a0469c4-9fde-58cd-b4e8-93cc3472dd78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-7,-5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299401} {:answer/id #uuid "3b0b858d-3e2e-508a-905e-95331611e4f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5,7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299402} {:answer/id #uuid "6efd377a-dfbe-5590-a3f6-46ec259d6f48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-7,-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c84f2aa-2f8e-5a59-b160-6da05be9ee04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299400} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b50ee55-ea0c-53be-9ecd-3166557c26c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b1ab664-b962-5c4e-81a6-13869e553585" :question/math-academy-id "q-181773" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={n\\in N:|n+6|<1}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $|n+6|\\le 1.$ So, we first need to solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|n+6|<1 \\\\ -1<n+6<1 \\\\ -7<n<-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above inequality does not have natural solutions.\n\nTherefore, the set $A$ is a null set:\n\n$$\nA=∅.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2ae57a-fde8-5d07-bbff-e66fbd4428b0" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Absolute Value Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a016b5f-55b2-576d-a903-79929a3dab9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,1,2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299406} {:answer/id #uuid "0931d67d-1da1-5654-a3b8-7bc4dc30739f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299407} {:answer/id #uuid "27f9061e-792b-54a2-b411-aa1862e27b4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299408} {:answer/id #uuid "f0e26beb-01a6-501d-aac4-0bd763fc6b53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,\\pm 1,2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299409} {:answer/id #uuid "a37c4d99-889e-55ce-b8c5-e41c86f32a59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-1,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0e26beb-01a6-501d-aac4-0bd763fc6b53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,\\pm 1,2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299409} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6c132bb-62a0-5813-b48a-1f56132e27e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c890544-9364-570c-8c45-b8d5bb680f83" :question/math-academy-id "q-181782" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={k\\in Z:|4k-2|\\le 6}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the integer numbers that satisfy the inequality $|4k-2|\\le 6.$ So, we first need to solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|4k-2|\\le 6 \\\\ -6\\le 4k-2\\le 6 \\\\ -4\\le 4k\\le 8 \\\\ -1\\le k\\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the above inequality are $-1,0,1,2.$ \n\nTherefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA={0,\\pm 1,2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74611c25-8501-52a7-a705-b7e9f8f6b8ee" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Trigonometric Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8199092d-859d-518f-9ff5-de7cffeea732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{…,-\\frac{7}{2},-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{9}{2},…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299413} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a08471-b420-50b3-be16-9e125cba0f35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299414} {:answer/id #uuid "0ba434b4-f118-5b68-8759-790b12875512" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\pm \\frac{5}{2},\\pm \\frac{7}{2},…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299415} {:answer/id #uuid "0dd7de0d-2a23-57d0-b527-9c73841eb321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299416} {:answer/id #uuid "88284a20-7e1f-5ddf-b821-c03c6d29a54b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{7}{2},…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8199092d-859d-518f-9ff5-de7cffeea732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{…,-\\frac{7}{2},-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{9}{2},…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299413} :answer-field/id #uuid "36375cc1-4239-507e-a424-18416539eea9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f59fc09f-c428-55b5-a5ab-1134651f23b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-181784" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in Q\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)=1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pi x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ \\pi x & =\\pi (\\frac{1}{2}+2n) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}+2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=…,-\\frac{7}{2},-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{9}{2},…\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={…,-\\frac{7}{2},-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{9}{2},…}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74611c25-8501-52a7-a705-b7e9f8f6b8ee" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Trigonometric Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ea75d78-3080-5e68-a933-428927c67284" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299420} {:answer/id #uuid "7555f3bb-db32-5a4d-9484-ec2151a98145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299421} {:answer/id #uuid "dfa3c2ae-01e9-52ad-b40e-6329a9c8d132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299422} {:answer/id #uuid "de488b30-d34f-51e7-a97d-e3256c424287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299423} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7dd0dd-c4bb-5d7a-bbdc-e8dc12cf585d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfa3c2ae-01e9-52ad-b40e-6329a9c8d132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299422} :answer-field/id #uuid "a23e8b6c-9737-5db8-9eb4-88736f76a77a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f3e31501-59b7-5807-a5bb-b8096c3b5c0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-181786" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=-1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=-1\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =\\pi +2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,…}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299425 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739c04ac-6d0c-5173-aa91-b5cc4dec8128" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Quadratic Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee4276f9-f32c-5c9d-88de-434471973e02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299427} {:answer/id #uuid "ad0f8667-6ebb-573a-82f8-611fd31b2daf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm 3\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299428} {:answer/id #uuid "a91dec3e-d6e2-5ddf-ac84-db477184d445" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299429} {:answer/id #uuid "c0bd6417-6f73-50b3-95d2-d0e3a2f3aac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299430} {:answer/id #uuid "3e201c33-d9d1-5dbf-868d-19132864441b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee4276f9-f32c-5c9d-88de-434471973e02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299427} :answer-field/id #uuid "52bb0371-b133-5d63-828b-ae8097f44902" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b75d7278-54cd-556d-b8b6-9bd7cc52dc48" :question/math-academy-id "q-181790" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:3{x}^{2}+27=0}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the real numbers that satisfy the equation $3{x}^{2}+27=0.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+27 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & =-27 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-9 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{-9} \\\\ x & =\\pm 3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $x\\in R$ and $\\pm 3\\text{i}\\notin R,$ we conclude that the set $A$ contains no elements. Hence, $A=∅.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299432 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739c04ac-6d0c-5173-aa91-b5cc4dec8128" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Quadratic Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d58b0f05-0bca-5042-8fac-55fbec2775ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299434} {:answer/id #uuid "74456efd-6682-5249-a118-8ff1a13ad465" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299435} {:answer/id #uuid "ce488cd9-f835-560c-9c71-b23c7188f047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299436} {:answer/id #uuid "63fbde89-a0cf-502f-80c7-a89235d1c452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299437} {:answer/id #uuid "a6f97a23-5852-5e57-916e-889480d97adc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63fbde89-a0cf-502f-80c7-a89235d1c452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1,2,3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299437} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c2c3042-fc85-52dc-8568-da7dfb0ae987" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fea999a1-ecb1-5af7-8aab-a0e696475ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-181794" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={n\\in N:2{n}^{2}-30<2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $2{n}^{2}-30<2.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{n}^{2}-30 & <2 \\\\ 2{n}^{2} & <32 \\\\ {n}^{2} & <16 \\\\ \\sqrt{{n}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{16} \\\\ |n| & <4 \\\\ -4<n & <4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe natural numbers that are solutions to the inequality above are $1,2,3.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA={1,2,3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299439 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74611c25-8501-52a7-a705-b7e9f8f6b8ee" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Trigonometric Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26ff209a-ad93-5267-85a6-a5b0c754cd41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,\\,\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\pi ,\\,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299441} {:answer/id #uuid "59ef3ceb-aa68-55bb-b893-456717b5ac0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299442} {:answer/id #uuid "41d84eb7-6cb4-599f-837e-a09056628cbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pi ,\\,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299443} {:answer/id #uuid "af3aeb11-a995-57eb-afe5-e7633bbcabd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299444} {:answer/id #uuid "2d092794-2b6e-5027-a993-00545c50504c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,\\,\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26ff209a-ad93-5267-85a6-a5b0c754cd41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0,\\,\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\pi ,\\,…}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299441} :answer-field/id #uuid "76f36de7-0143-5ca9-a77e-fe5d8e8a1d67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d030d9d-630d-5fc3-842b-16fbcac63c14" :question/math-academy-id "q-181795" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R\\,:\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4x)=0}?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4x)=0\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\pi ,\\,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={0,\\,\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\pi ,\\,…}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739c04ac-6d0c-5173-aa91-b5cc4dec8128" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Quadratic Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5cf150b-57cf-52e9-9201-ff98b3c79e67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299448} {:answer/id #uuid "4e088928-3ac8-5405-ae2c-7bf671ebf524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299449} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2a3340-de5d-5874-99c0-b91401a3dba5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pm 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299450} {:answer/id #uuid "7958f79e-6dc3-5cde-96bf-7f952ea6d8c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{-}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299451} {:answer/id #uuid "df66b022-fa8c-5bc6-aba1-ffa0ae7bb95c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df66b022-fa8c-5bc6-aba1-ffa0ae7bb95c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299452} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfe66415-f3a3-5ce3-8de8-f2ff06aec424" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e5616ed2-c161-5c96-8b53-7dd0a0fa6f9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-181799" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in {R}^{-}:3{x}^{2}\\le 27}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the negative real numbers that satisfy the inequality $3{x}^{2}\\le 27.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2} & \\le 27 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\le 9 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\le \\sqrt{9} \\\\ |x| & \\le 3 \\\\ -3\\le x & \\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe negative real numbers that are solutions to the inequality above are $x\\in [-3,0).$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA=[-3,0).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739c04ac-6d0c-5173-aa91-b5cc4dec8128" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Quadratic Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9a86188-202c-5bda-b11d-428e9e443610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{0}^{+}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299455} {:answer/id #uuid "d90dd0fc-0ebc-5d7c-bd54-f81f5391deab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299456} {:answer/id #uuid "a596cc0c-06c7-526f-8d3a-39b67067c4f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{+}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299457} {:answer/id #uuid "4a66601d-f4cc-5316-898f-c127e65d6d3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299458} {:answer/id #uuid "6c8b1997-3513-5e00-b39f-ee28db3104ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a66601d-f4cc-5316-898f-c127e65d6d3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299458} :answer-field/id #uuid "73d642b5-fd73-51aa-87f5-d6fbe003177c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6599a085-eb62-54ba-8230-37cab557b7e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-181803" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in {R}_{0}^{+}:9{x}^{2}+4\\le 4}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the positive real numbers and zero that satisfy the inequality $9{x}^{2}+4\\le 4.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}+4 & \\le 4 \\\\ 9{x}^{2} & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only solution to the inequality above that is in ${R}_{0}^{+}$ is $x=0.$ Therefore, $A={0}.$"}]}
